{
  "slug": "setsail",
  "family": "tracks",
  "label": "Set Sail Anthem",
  "note": "original — written in the idiom of the One Piece opening 「ウィーアー!」(Kohei Tanaka, 1999), not transcribed from it or from any score. B flat major, 157.5 BPM (rowLen 2100, rows are 32nds so one pattern is one bar), 21 bars, loops at exactly 32 s. 4-bar horn fanfare Bb Eb F Bb, 8-bar verse Bb Gm Eb F / Bb Gm Cm F, 8-bar chorus a fourth up Eb F Dm Gm / Eb F Bb F, and a 1-bar F tag that walks back into the fanfare. 7 ch: anthem_lead = the tune (silent through the fanfare, verse in C5-G5, chorus peaking on C6 at bar 18), horn_call = the fanfare alone up front, a held tone under the verse, then two-note answers in the chorus rests, power_chunk = off-beat eighth stabs between the lead's beats, drive_bass = eighths that never rest with a chromatic approach into each bar, bass_drum_3 / snare_1 / open_hihat = the kit, snare rolls closing bars 4, 12, 20 and 21, tambourine opening up to six hits a bar in the chorus.",
